# Ooda CLI — Editor Setup

File: ooda/docs/CLI_SETUP.oot

The `ooda` binary is the unified meta-router for the openOODA tactical toolchain. It is one program with one stable name and one argv surface. Editors, agents, CI scripts, and humans all call the same binary. This file documents what you need to make `ooda` run on a host.

## What ooda is

`ooda` is the ooda/ repo's single deliverable. The source tree has 4 in-process command groups (build, fix, fmt, token) and 3 external-package spawns (opm, lsp, mcp). The compiled binary is small and has no shared library state at runtime beyond the spawned subprocesses. The dispatch table lives in `ooda/main.oo` and totals under 100 lines.

## How ooda is installed

There are two install paths. Both are acceptable; pick the one that matches the deployment model.

### Install path A — pack install (the standard)

The ooda/ repo ships an `ooda install` command. It is the post-build step that takes a pre-built openOODA release pack and lays it out under an XDG-style prefix.

```sh
# After building a pack
ooda install --from ./build/pack --to $HOME
source $HOME/.config/ooda/env
```

The install command requires `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` to be set. It refuses paths outside that writedir. It also refuses `--from` paths that fail the pack validation check (need `bin/ooda`, `ooda/oodac_bin`, `std`, `runtime`, `fixtures/hello.oo`).

### Install path B — install repo (the canonical)

The `openOODA/install` repo has `install.sh` that pulls ooda/, oodac, std, runtime, and fixtures, then calls the same `ooda install` command internally. This is the path the website uses. It is not this subcommand.

In both paths the post-condition is identical: the host has `$PREFIX/.local/bin/ooda` on `$PATH` and a `$PREFIX/.config/ooda/env` file that exports the 5 OODA_* vars. Editors and shells should `source` that env file.

## Cap requirements

The `ooda` binary is granted 8 caps by its host at startup: `BindCap`, `FsReadCap`, `ProcessCap`, `SysCap`, `EnvCap`, `TimeCap`, `FsWriteCap`, `AllocCap`. Each subcommand requests only the caps it needs; the runtime enforces a least-privilege gate at the call site.

| Cap        | Granted | Used by |
|------------|---------|---------|
| BindCap    | yes     | startup; one-shot |
| FsReadCap  | yes     | every subcommand that reads source, configs, or tree listings |
| ProcessCap | yes     | build, run, test, bench, install, fix, token (any command that invokes oodac or chmod) |
| SysCap     | yes     | main entry only; reserved for future low-level syscalls |
| EnvCap     | yes     | every subcommand that resolves the compiler or reads OODA_* |
| TimeCap    | yes     | bench, test (for unique per-invocation artifact names), token |
| FsWriteCap | yes     | build, run, install, fix, gen, init, fmt, token, digest |
| AllocCap   | yes     | fmt (for builder alloc), reserved for others |

Commands that do not need a cap simply do not take it. The current main signature in `ooda/main.oo` takes all 8 because the compile-time type system does not yet let you split the cap list per branch.

## Environment at runtime

The 5 vars ooda reads at startup are the prefix vars set by the install step: `OODA_HOME`, `OODA_SRC_ROOT`, `OODA_STD`, `OODA_CONFIG`, `OODA_CACHE`. Beyond those, the runtime reads:

- `OODACODEX` — optional override for the spawned-binary search dir.
- `OODA_COMPILER` — required compiler path.
- `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` — required by `install`; gates the install writedir.
- `OODA_FS_READDIR` — readonly source dir for the reproducible-build path.
- `OODA_HOME`, `OODA_SRC_ROOT` — written by install; not used to find oodac.
- `OODA_CHECKOUT` — fallback for `--from` in `install` when the arg is absent.
- `OODA_VERSION` — written into the install receipt.

See `docs/ENV.oot` for the full env-var table.

## The 4 in-process subdirs

The ooda/ tree is 4 subdirs. Each subdir groups one family of commands. The `ooda` binary is the only host for the in-process commands; nothing else in the polyrepo runs them.

| Subdir | Subcommands | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| build/ | build, run, gen, test, install, bench, init, context, health | toolchain driver + project lifecycle |
| fix/   | fix, digest  | text-level edit + sha256 |
| fmt/   | fmt          | idempotent in-place formatter |
| token/ | token (12 sub-subcommands) | capability-token accounting |

## The 3 external packages (spawned)

| Subcommand | Binary | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `ooda opm <sub>` | `opm` | package manager (add, audit, ingest, launch) |
| `ooda lsp`       | `lsp` | LSP server over stdio JSON-RPC |
| `ooda mcp`       | `mcp` | MCP server over stdio JSON-RPC |

Spawn requires `OODACODEX`. The bin is `$OODACODEX/bin/<name>` only. Stdio is inherited. See `docs/dispatch.oot`.
